  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "A",
  "Solution": "A product of odd integers is odd, so both \\(3^{11}\\) and \\(5^{13}\\) are odd. The sum of two odd integers is even, which means \\(2\\) divides \\(3^{11}+5^{13}\\). Since \\(2\\) is the smallest prime number, the requested prime is \\(\\boxed{2}\\), choice \\(\\mathrm{A}\\).",
